      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racine%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Racine was platted in 1890, marking the start of its formal development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racine%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Racine is drained to the east by unnamed tributaries of Bear Creek, part of the Root River watershed flowing to the Mississippi River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racine%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Racine is surrounded by Racine Township but remains an independent municipality, a unique arrangement in the region.",
